WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.966
Cha-cha, lucha!

2
00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:07.033
Cha, Hawlucha! -Noi.

3
00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.866
Noibat. Noi.

4
00:00:10.833 --> 00:00:12.000
Noibat!

5
00:00:12.066 --> 00:00:15.666
- You can do it, Noibat, go.
- Pika, pika.

6
00:00:15.733 --> 00:00:18.166
Noibat, bat! Noi!

7
00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:23.400
While our heroes continue their journey to Anistar City,

8
00:00:23.466 --> 00:00:27.233
they pause to do a little aerial training with Noibat.

9
00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:30.866
Noibat's riding the wind. Its long-range flying is better.

10
00:00:30.933 --> 00:00:33.733
All this training's really starting to pay off.

11
00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:38.433
- Denne-ne! Denne-ne-ne-ne!
- Huh? You want to fly too, Dedenne?

12
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:39.733
Denne.

13
00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:42.866
That's how it's done. And now try to flap your wings.

14
00:00:42.933 --> 00:00:46.633
- Bat, bat, bat, bat! Noi, Noibat!
- Fletchinder.

15
00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:49.800
Noi. Noibat.

16
00:00:49.866 --> 00:00:51.100
That's it, Fletchinder.

17
00:00:51.166 --> 00:00:53.733
Just copy its movements, Noibat. Keep it up.

18
00:00:54.866 --> 00:00:56.966
Noi, Noibat, bat!

19
00:00:57.033 --> 00:00:58.000
-Pika!

20
00:00:58.066 --> 00:01:00.766
- Hang in there, Noibat!
- Pikachu!

21
00:01:00.833 --> 00:01:03.733
- Noi, noi, Noibat!
- Lucha!

22
00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:05.500
Noibat!

23
00:01:05.566 --> 00:01:07.700
Haaaa!

24
00:01:07.766 --> 00:01:10.966
Noi-oi! Noibat!

25
00:01:12.966 --> 00:01:14.966
Bat!

26
00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:16.066
- That's amazing.
- Pika!

27
00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:18.700
Wow, Hawlucha's really setting a great example.

28
00:01:18.766 --> 00:01:20.833
- Yes! You're doing great.
- Pika!

29
00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:23.733
Noi! Bat, Noibat.

30
00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:25.833
You see, Noibat? You can fly.

31
00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:28.266
Now all you have to do is remember that stuff.

32
00:01:28.333 --> 00:01:30.866
Noi!

33
00:01:30.933 --> 00:01:32.133
Noibat!

34
00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:40.133
- Noibat can sure express its joy loudly.
- Noibat!

35
00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.633
You're gonna be OK.

36
00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:45.066
- Strong Pokémon don't cry.
- Pikachu.

37
00:01:45.133 --> 00:01:47.133
-Noi.

38
00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.433
- Cha.
- Chinder.

39
00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:50.666
See that?

40
00:01:50.733 --> 00:01:54.500
Hawlucha and Fletchinder want you to know they're behind you all the way.

41
00:01:54.566 --> 00:01:56.166
- Hawlucha.
- Fletchinder.

42
00:01:58.533 --> 00:02:01.433
Noi. Noibat.

43
00:02:05.833 --> 00:02:06.866
Who were they?

44
00:02:06.933 --> 00:02:09.766
That was Starly, Staravia, and Staraptor.

45
00:02:09.833 --> 00:02:13.933
- Wow, they sure are fast.
- Pika. Pikachu.

46
00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.800
♪ You're just a kid on a quest ♪

47
00:02:15.866 --> 00:02:17.566
♪ To be the best of the best ♪

48
00:02:17.633 --> 00:02:21.000
♪ Someday you're destined for power and glory ♪

49
00:02:21.066 --> 00:02:22.466
♪ You know you're up to the test ♪

50
00:02:22.533 --> 00:02:26.300
♪ There's only one way to tell this story ♪

51
00:02:26.366 --> 00:02:29.566
♪ Be a hero! Be a hero! ♪

52
00:02:29.633 --> 00:02:33.000
♪ All the power is at your command ♪

53
00:02:33.066 --> 00:02:36.966
♪ Face your fears and show you're a hero ♪

54
00:02:37.033 --> 00:02:41.666
♪ The future of the world is in your hand! ♪

55
00:02:41.733 --> 00:02:43.933
♪ Pokémon! ♪

56
00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:50.633
A Relay in the Sky!

57
00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:55.933
You've come to the right place. Welcome.

58
00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:59.866
Step right up everyone. Come on, enjoy the fun.

59
00:02:59.933 --> 00:03:02.766
Wow, look at all of them.

60
00:03:02.833 --> 00:03:05.866
Pidgeotto, Butterfree and Swoobat are here too.

61
00:03:05.933 --> 00:03:09.100
There are so many Pokémon that fly, all here together.

62
00:03:09.166 --> 00:03:11.500
Maybe it's some kind of contest.

63
00:03:11.566 --> 00:03:14.366
It feels a little bit like a Rhyhorn race.

64
00:03:14.433 --> 00:03:16.633
It's a Pokémon Sky Relay.

65
00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:21.833
What's a Pokémon Sky Relay?

66
00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:25.400
You mean you came all the way out here and you don't even know what it is?

67
00:03:25.466 --> 00:03:27.600
Nope. See, we're on a journey.

68
00:03:27.666 --> 00:03:30.466
- Uh, my name is Ash.
- Pikachu.

69
00:03:30.533 --> 00:03:31.666
Hawlucha.

70
00:03:31.733 --> 00:03:33.733
- Noibat, Noibat.
- Fletchinder.

71
00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:37.266
- I'm Serena. Hello, there.
- I'm Bonnie.

72
00:03:37.333 --> 00:03:40.866
Dedenne's right in here. That's my big brother.

73
00:03:40.933 --> 00:03:42.600
Hello, there. I'm Clemont.

74
00:03:42.666 --> 00:03:44.100
- Heh.
- Denne-ne!

75
00:03:44.166 --> 00:03:48.633
I'm Ornithol. And to my right is my partner, Noctowl.

76
00:03:49.933 --> 00:03:53.233
A Noctowl! Hi, there.

77
00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:55.933
Wow. You look exactly like Ornithol.

78
00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.100
- Denne-ne!
- Heh.

79
00:03:58.166 --> 00:04:00.933
So what is it? The Pokémon Sky Relay?

80
00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:04.500
Well, the Pokémon Sky Relay is a flying competition

81
00:04:04.566 --> 00:04:07.900
between teams made up of three flying Pokémon each.

82
00:04:07.966 --> 00:04:11.933
These Pokémon come from all around to show that they're the bigwigs,

83
00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.100
or should I say big wings, of the Sky Relay.

84
00:04:15.166 --> 00:04:19.633
- Wow.
- We saw those three before.

85
00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:22.833
- Star!
- Star!

86
00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:26.133
Nice flying out there. You're looking really great.

87
00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:29.633
Best of luck to you tomorrow.

88
00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:32.866
- I'll bet you that guy is their trainer.
- Pika, pika.

89
00:04:32.933 --> 00:04:36.166
His name is Orson. He's the previous Sky Relay winner.

90
00:04:36.233 --> 00:04:40.600
His team is made up of Starly, Staravia, and Staraptor.

91
00:04:40.666 --> 00:04:43.366
Of course, he's looking for back-to-back wins.

92
00:04:43.433 --> 00:04:48.366
- Ash, are those three Pokémon with you?
- Oh yeah. They sure are.

93
00:04:48.433 --> 00:04:50.866
Hm?

94
00:04:50.933 --> 00:04:52.933
Noi!

95
00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.366
Hacha!

96
00:04:54.433 --> 00:04:57.600
That's what I call spirit. I like that.

97
00:04:57.666 --> 00:05:02.166
So, how about this? Why don't you enter the Pokémon Sky Relay too?

98
00:05:02.233 --> 00:05:04.400
- Wait. Us?
- Pika?

99
00:05:04.466 --> 00:05:06.833
I'm asking you to join me in my dream

100
00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:09.933
to take the victory in the Pokémon Sky Relay, see?

101
00:05:11.466 --> 00:05:15.033
- Wow. Maybe we should do it, guys.
- Ash, are you sure?

102
00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:16.700
- Huh?
- Noibat, too?

103
00:05:16.766 --> 00:05:19.133
Yeah. Sounds like lots of fun to me.

104
00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:21.633
So that means you agree to do it.

105
00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:24.333
Great. We'll win the Sky Relay together.

106
00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:25.633
- Right.
- Pika!

107
00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:29.066
Hey, Noibat, this is perfect for some real training.

108
00:05:29.133 --> 00:05:30.400
Bat, bat, Noibat.

109
00:05:30.466 --> 00:05:33.633
- Yeah. It'll be great.
- Pika, pika!

110
00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:35.633
-Fletchinder!

111
00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:37.666
They're sure excited about their dumb plan.

112
00:05:37.733 --> 00:05:38.766
You're right.

113
00:05:38.833 --> 00:05:42.266
Putting that Noibat in the Pokémon Sky Relay doesn't get much dumber.

114
00:05:42.333 --> 00:05:44.300
They are the twerps, after all.

115
00:05:44.366 --> 00:05:47.633
But maybe those dopes are gonna wind up givin' us our big chance.

116
00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:49.366
What are you talking about?

117
00:05:49.433 --> 00:05:52.966
A tough race like the Sky Relay might sharpen Noibat up.

118
00:05:53.033 --> 00:05:55.233
- And then what?
- I know!

119
00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:59.066
Noibat gets stronger and then evolves, right? Of course.

120
00:05:59.133 --> 00:06:01.733
- We'll scoop that baby up.
- I see.

121
00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:04.866
Which means we're going to have to get involved in this as well.

122
00:06:04.933 --> 00:06:10.033
- What does get involved mean?
- It's obvious. We enter the relay too.

123
00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:13.766
We chase after Noibat and the moment it evolves, we grab it.

124
00:06:13.833 --> 00:06:14.833
Hold the phone.

125
00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:19.266
The Sky Relay requires three Flying Pokémon in order to establish a team.

126
00:06:19.333 --> 00:06:23.033
We've already got Pumpkaboo and Inkay, but we need three to make a trio.

127
00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:26.400
- Do the math.
- Don't worry your troubled head.

128
00:06:26.466 --> 00:06:30.200
When it comes to scientific equipment, Team Rocket's on the cutting edge.

129
00:06:30.266 --> 00:06:32.600
Wobbuffet!

130
00:06:33.666 --> 00:06:37.266
Now, let's look at a map of the Pokémon Sky Relay course.

131
00:06:37.333 --> 00:06:38.666
Here's the starting line.

132
00:06:38.733 --> 00:06:42.766
The starting Pokémon wears a sash and flies the first leg of the course

133
00:06:42.833 --> 00:06:46.266
with the trainer giving directions from a balloon high above.

134
00:06:46.333 --> 00:06:48.000
The second Pokémon is here.

135
00:06:48.066 --> 00:06:52.300
It receives the sash at the edge of the forest and then circles around the cliff.

136
00:06:52.366 --> 00:06:55.333
Finally, it passes the sash off to the anchor.

137
00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:57.300
The finish line is back at the start.

138
00:06:57.366 --> 00:07:01.033
And that's where we will find out which team wins.

139
00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:05.966
OK. We're gonna start the first leg with Fletchinder.

140
00:07:06.033 --> 00:07:08.633
- Chinder.
- Hawlucha's next. Got it?

141
00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:11.933
- Ha!
- Noibat, you're going to be the anchor.

142
00:07:12.566 --> 00:07:14.933
Noi, noi! Noibat!

143
00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:17.633
Ah, yes. Flying freely through the sky.

144
00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:19.966
The eternal dream of humankind.

145
00:07:20.033 --> 00:07:24.133
And the Sky Relay is where we entrust that dream to our Pokémon,

146
00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:28.400
strengthening the bond between people and Pokémon with an unending friendship.

147
00:07:28.466 --> 00:07:32.900
- That's what the Sky Relay's all about!
- Let's give it all we've got.

148
00:07:35.733 --> 00:07:39.033
I was wondering, have you competed in the relay before?

149
00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:42.666
I'll bet your goal has always been to be the best and win first prize

150
00:07:42.733 --> 00:07:45.266
and set unbeatable records for all time.

151
00:07:45.333 --> 00:07:48.033
Sorry, but I've never done any of that.

152
00:07:49.333 --> 00:07:53.000
I've never participated in the Sky Relay even once.

153
00:07:53.066 --> 00:07:56.100
- But, wait, how can that be true?
- That's weird.

154
00:07:56.166 --> 00:07:59.233
- You love the Sky Relay, don't you?
- Denne-ne.

155
00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:02.366
Yes. I love it more than anything.

156
00:08:02.433 --> 00:08:05.800
But you see, the real truth is...

157
00:08:05.866 --> 00:08:08.733
- What is it?
- Pika?

158
00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:10.833
Ugh, the real truth is

159
00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:14.400
I was never actually able to catch three Flying Pokémon.

160
00:08:14.466 --> 00:08:16.033
-Pika!

161
00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:20.333
Well, I couldn't be part of the Sky Relay with only Noctowl, right?

162
00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:22.633
That's why I was hoping I could get the help

163
00:08:22.700 --> 00:08:25.266
and support of strong trainers just like you.

164
00:08:25.333 --> 00:08:28.766
- OK, now I get it.
- Pikachu.

165
00:08:28.833 --> 00:08:31.766
Actual racing experience may have eluded me,

166
00:08:31.833 --> 00:08:35.266
but I haven't been watching all these many years for nothin'.

167
00:08:35.333 --> 00:08:36.966
I'm beggin' you, Ash.

168
00:08:37.033 --> 00:08:39.766
Won't you help my dream come true?

169
00:08:39.833 --> 00:08:41.400
Right.

170
00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:51.933
We've got great weather here today.

171
00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:54.866
A perfect day for the Pokémon Sky Relay.

172
00:08:54.933 --> 00:08:58.366
The Pokémon have finished their warm-ups,

173
00:08:58.433 --> 00:09:03.333
and one by one, their trainers are starting to climb aboard their balloons.

174
00:09:06.233 --> 00:09:09.600
And now, the Pokémon for the second leg have assumed their positions

175
00:09:09.666 --> 00:09:11.400
and are ready to go.

176
00:09:11.466 --> 00:09:14.633
The anchors are also waiting in their positions,

177
00:09:16.066 --> 00:09:20.000
as everyone anxiously waits for the signal to take flight.

178
00:09:21.066 --> 00:09:23.933
All teams' Pokémon, proceed to the starting line.

179
00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:26.600
Trainers, lift your balloons high into the air.

180
00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:30.733
Go get 'em, Fletchinder.

181
00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:32.833
- Pika, pika!
- Fletchinder.

182
00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:37.833
The balloons are on their way up and the countdown is about to start.

183
00:09:49.466 --> 00:09:51.900
And the first leg is off and flying.

184
00:09:51.966 --> 00:09:55.733
The thrilling Pokémon Sky Relay has begun.

185
00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:00.533
- Now, that was a great start.
- Aah!

186
00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:01.666
Let's keep it up.

187
00:10:01.733 --> 00:10:04.200
- Go, Fletchinder. Go, go, Fletchinder.
- Denne-ne-ne!

188
00:10:04.266 --> 00:10:05.833
- Go, Fletchinder. Yeah!
- Cha, lucha!

189
00:10:13.900 --> 00:10:17.900
- See that? Fletchinder's in the lead.
- Noibat.

190
00:10:20.966 --> 00:10:22.900
- Ah!
- Pikachu!

191
00:10:22.966 --> 00:10:26.200
Now, the start is the most important part of the race.

192
00:10:26.266 --> 00:10:28.900
That's where you get the first chance to take the lead.

193
00:10:28.966 --> 00:10:31.366
Then all the other Pokémon will see your back.

194
00:10:31.433 --> 00:10:33.666
Fletchinder, rock and roll.

195
00:10:33.733 --> 00:10:37.033
Fletchin, Fletchinder! Fletch!

196
00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:40.166
Fletchinder's in the lead

197
00:10:40.233 --> 00:10:43.433
and that means Team Ash is off to a rousing start!

198
00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:46.933
- Fletchinder, way to go.
- Pika, pika!

199
00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:50.000
Who's that Pokémon?

200
00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:56.533
It's Noctowl.

201
00:11:01.566 --> 00:11:03.666
The Pokémon have now reached the forest.

202
00:11:03.733 --> 00:11:06.133
One by one, they're heading into the trees.

203
00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:09.900
Fletch! Fletchinder! Fletchinder!

204
00:11:13.166 --> 00:11:16.000
Combee, come on. Show me some speed.

205
00:11:16.066 --> 00:11:18.000
Give it all you've got, Ninjask.

206
00:11:18.066 --> 00:11:21.000
- Great. Keep it up, Fletchinder.
- Pika, pika!

207
00:11:21.066 --> 00:11:24.433
Now we come to the point where you enter the great forest.

208
00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:27.166
Exceptional mobility is the key.

209
00:11:27.233 --> 00:11:29.866
Looking ahead while flying is paramount.

210
00:11:29.933 --> 00:11:32.233
Any drop in speed, and you haven't got a chance.

211
00:11:37.266 --> 00:11:38.766
- What's going on? Is that allowed?
- Pika!

212
00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:40.500
Dreigon.

213
00:11:42.433 --> 00:11:43.666
Combee!

214
00:11:46.966 --> 00:11:48.533
Dreigon...

215
00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:51.800
- Aah!
- Pika.

216
00:11:51.866 --> 00:11:56.533
One must always expect the unexpected. It's all part of the thrill.

217
00:11:56.600 --> 00:12:00.200
Staravia, drop your speed. Look everywhere around you.

218
00:12:00.266 --> 00:12:02.833
Now, Altaria. Take the lead.

219
00:12:02.900 --> 00:12:04.800
Star! Staravia!

220
00:12:06.733 --> 00:12:08.666
Fletch! Fletchinder!

221
00:12:11.066 --> 00:12:12.933
We have a new leader.

222
00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:19.000
Altaria has moved into first place, with Staravia right on its tail.

223
00:12:19.066 --> 00:12:21.900
We've lost the lead but we're still in third place.

224
00:12:21.966 --> 00:12:24.133
- That's a good position to be in.
- Denne-ne.

225
00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:26.500
- Huh?
- Here comes Altaria. Look.

226
00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:30.400
- That's your cue.
- Pumpkaboo.

227
00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:33.000
Pumpka!

228
00:12:33.066 --> 00:12:35.233
- Huh?
- Hey, what's going on?

229
00:12:35.300 --> 00:12:39.200
Hiding in Altaria's wings to hijack first place. Genius.

230
00:12:39.266 --> 00:12:41.166
Our strategy is flawless.

231
00:12:41.233 --> 00:12:43.066
- You go get 'em, Meowth.
- Argh!

232
00:12:43.133 --> 00:12:45.033
Oops. I mean, Pelipper.

233
00:12:45.100 --> 00:12:47.866
Pumpkaboo has somehow managed to take the lead.

234
00:12:47.933 --> 00:12:52.033
Man, gotta get ahead of Hawlucha.

235
00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:55.466
And then, we get the twerp's Noibat.

236
00:12:59.433 --> 00:13:02.833
Starrrrrrravia!

237
00:13:02.900 --> 00:13:04.566
Staraptor!

238
00:13:04.633 --> 00:13:06.566
Staraptor!

239
00:13:07.566 --> 00:13:09.400
Fletchinder!

240
00:13:11.566 --> 00:13:13.066
You're up, Hawlucha.

241
00:13:13.133 --> 00:13:15.466
- Lucha, lu.
- Fletchinder!

242
00:13:15.533 --> 00:13:17.866
Ha-cha!

243
00:13:20.666 --> 00:13:22.400
- Get 'em, Hawlucha.
- Fletchinder.

244
00:13:22.466 --> 00:13:23.533
- Denne-ne!
- Fletchinder.

245
00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:28.466
Pelipper is still first,

246
00:13:28.533 --> 00:13:31.166
but Staraptor and Hawlucha are coming up fast.

247
00:13:31.233 --> 00:13:35.566
It looks like three teams have taken a big lead and left the others behind.

248
00:13:37.633 --> 00:13:42.166
The second leg is a challenging course that takes you between huge rocks.

249
00:13:42.233 --> 00:13:44.666
Being careful is of the utmost importance.

250
00:13:44.733 --> 00:13:48.433
Hey, do you think we actually have a chance of winning this thing?

251
00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:49.666
Chance?

252
00:13:49.733 --> 00:13:52.166
Of course. We'll grab the top spot

253
00:13:52.233 --> 00:13:54.166
and catch Noibat at the same time.

254
00:13:54.233 --> 00:13:58.866
Right on. We'll tag our target and get all the glory in one fell swoop.

255
00:13:58.933 --> 00:14:00.933
- Precisely.
- Turbo time.

256
00:14:04.733 --> 00:14:08.266
We can't fall behind any further. Quick. Go after it.

257
00:14:08.333 --> 00:14:10.766
Staraptor!

258
00:14:10.833 --> 00:14:12.666
- Star! Star! Star!
- Heads up. Dodge it.

259
00:14:12.733 --> 00:14:14.666
Staraptor!

260
00:14:14.733 --> 00:14:17.900
Staraptor is unable to close the gap with Pelipper.

261
00:14:17.966 --> 00:14:22.400
- Yeah! Do it.
- Hawlucha. The rocks. Use the rocks!

262
00:14:22.466 --> 00:14:24.666
Lu!

263
00:14:24.733 --> 00:14:26.666
Cha! Ha!

264
00:14:29.833 --> 00:14:31.566
- Star?
- Aah!

265
00:14:31.633 --> 00:14:33.933
- Yeah!
- Pika!

266
00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:36.300
Haaaa...

267
00:14:36.366 --> 00:14:40.600
Hawlucha is actually using the rocks to close in on Pelipper.

268
00:14:40.666 --> 00:14:43.266
That's it! Take the lead!

269
00:14:43.333 --> 00:14:46.766
- How's Ash doing?
- Oh, Clemont. Wonderful.

270
00:14:46.833 --> 00:14:49.400
Hawlucha just caught up.

271
00:14:50.833 --> 00:14:53.766
Lu... cha...

272
00:14:53.833 --> 00:14:54.833
Argh!

273
00:14:54.900 --> 00:14:56.766
- Yes! Even.
- Pika!

274
00:14:56.833 --> 00:14:59.500
- Meowth, for the block.
- I rock.

275
00:14:59.566 --> 00:15:01.566
Lucha!

276
00:15:01.633 --> 00:15:03.700
- Ha!
- No way!

277
00:15:03.766 --> 00:15:05.066
Pika!

278
00:15:07.133 --> 00:15:10.566
- Oh, no. Is that legal?
- Noibat!

279
00:15:10.633 --> 00:15:13.100
Pelipper is delivering body blows

280
00:15:13.166 --> 00:15:15.300
and Team R is on the offensive.

281
00:15:15.366 --> 00:15:18.200
- Don't quit. Hang in there.
- Pika, pika!

282
00:15:18.266 --> 00:15:20.200
Ha?

283
00:15:21.766 --> 00:15:23.433
Cha-aaah!

284
00:15:23.500 --> 00:15:24.933
Aah! Hawlucha.

285
00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:27.933
Noi, Noibat!

286
00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:29.700
Chu-la-ha!

287
00:15:29.766 --> 00:15:31.433
Ha-cha!

288
00:15:31.500 --> 00:15:33.933
I've had enough of that show-off.

289
00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:36.666
Hawlucha, dodge it.

290
00:15:36.733 --> 00:15:39.666
Lucha!

291
00:15:39.733 --> 00:15:41.666
Pika?

292
00:15:41.733 --> 00:15:44.166
- Pelipper broke apart?
- Noibat?

293
00:15:49.766 --> 00:15:51.300
Pelipper? What's going on?

294
00:15:52.733 --> 00:15:55.200
Prepare for trouble, you twerps. Hooray!

295
00:15:55.266 --> 00:15:57.533
Make mine a double and you will pay!

296
00:15:59.966 --> 00:16:01.966
- Huh? Team Rocket?
- Pika?

297
00:16:05.266 --> 00:16:06.933
What in the world is going on here?

298
00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:10.166
I think Pelipper just turned into something else.

299
00:16:10.233 --> 00:16:15.100
- Clemont, was that Team Rocket?
- Hey, what's a Team Rocket?

300
00:16:15.166 --> 00:16:19.300
Really bad guys who try to steal other people's Pokémon all the time.

301
00:16:19.366 --> 00:16:20.600
Denne-ne-ne!

302
00:16:22.666 --> 00:16:24.000
- What was that?
- Wob?

303
00:16:25.733 --> 00:16:27.600
-Team Rocket?

304
00:16:27.666 --> 00:16:29.466
It's the same old story.

305
00:16:29.533 --> 00:16:31.333
- No target!
- No glory!

306
00:16:31.400 --> 00:16:33.533
We're blasting off again!

307
00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:35.500
Wobbuffet!

308
00:16:38.466 --> 00:16:39.933
Ha.

309
00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:44.133
- Lucha!
- Bat!

310
00:16:44.200 --> 00:16:48.366
- Ash, what was that all about?
- Team Rocket, but it's OK now.

311
00:16:48.433 --> 00:16:51.100
- You ready, Noibat?
- Noibat!

312
00:16:51.166 --> 00:16:54.366
- Yeah. Then take off.
- Pika, pika!

313
00:16:55.666 --> 00:16:57.866
Bat, bat, bat!

314
00:16:57.933 --> 00:16:59.600
Staraptor!

315
00:16:59.666 --> 00:17:03.400
Go, Starly. And get as close to Noibat as you possibly can.

316
00:17:03.466 --> 00:17:05.566
Starly!

317
00:17:06.966 --> 00:17:10.566
Team R has been disqualified for violation of the rules.

318
00:17:10.633 --> 00:17:14.400
Which means the battle is now between Team Ash and Team Orson,

319
00:17:14.466 --> 00:17:17.900
and the anchor leg between Noibat and Starly will decide it all.

320
00:17:19.966 --> 00:17:21.666
All right, Noibat, you can do it!

321
00:17:21.733 --> 00:17:24.933
Noi! Noi! Noibat!

322
00:17:25.966 --> 00:17:30.100
Now, the third leg is fairly easy. Pretty much a straight line.

323
00:17:30.166 --> 00:17:32.500
Even Noibat should do well.

324
00:17:34.066 --> 00:17:36.033
Starly!

325
00:17:37.166 --> 00:17:39.533
Here comes Starly. Stay alert.

326
00:17:40.133 --> 00:17:42.033
Noi!

327
00:17:47.733 --> 00:17:52.500
Noibat is in the lead and Team Ash is poised to win it all.

328
00:17:52.566 --> 00:17:55.933
Not there yet. They've got to stay focused.

329
00:17:57.300 --> 00:17:59.533
Noibat, no doubt you can do it.

330
00:17:59.600 --> 00:18:03.266
But wind currents in the valley can change wildly before you know it.

331
00:18:03.333 --> 00:18:07.133
They can go from peaceful and calm to completely out of control.

332
00:18:12.666 --> 00:18:14.600
Noi! Noibat!

333
00:18:14.666 --> 00:18:16.800
- Huh? No, Noibat!
- Huh? It's a wind gust.

334
00:18:16.866 --> 00:18:17.833
Denne-ne-ne!

335
00:18:17.900 --> 00:18:20.833
- Noibat...
- Starly, fold your wings.

336
00:18:20.900 --> 00:18:23.333
Star! Starly!

337
00:18:23.400 --> 00:18:26.466
Noi! Noibat!

338
00:18:26.533 --> 00:18:30.066
- Noibat's falling down.
- You've gotta get it together, OK?

339
00:18:30.133 --> 00:18:31.600
Straighten up and fly right.

340
00:18:31.666 --> 00:18:33.700
- Pika, pika!
- Cha, ha-cha!

341
00:18:34.700 --> 00:18:35.933
Noi...

342
00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:40.466
Noibat will be just great. All of you just wait and see.

343
00:18:40.533 --> 00:18:42.066
Noi.

344
00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:45.600
- Lucha!
- Noibat!

345
00:18:46.300 --> 00:18:48.666
Haaaaa!

346
00:18:50.666 --> 00:18:52.700
Noibat!

347
00:18:53.433 --> 00:18:55.033
Noi!

348
00:18:55.766 --> 00:18:58.066
It looks like we have a race once again.

349
00:18:58.133 --> 00:19:00.366
Noibat's back in the game and closing in fast.

350
00:19:00.433 --> 00:19:02.833
Who will be number one?

351
00:19:02.900 --> 00:19:04.500
Noi, noi!

352
00:19:09.166 --> 00:19:11.933
- Pika!
- Go!

353
00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:14.966
- Cha!
- Go!

354
00:19:15.033 --> 00:19:17.933
- Go!
- Go!

355
00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:20.600
Yeah! You can do it!

356
00:19:20.666 --> 00:19:22.466
Noibat!

357
00:19:28.033 --> 00:19:29.766
Starly held on.

358
00:19:29.833 --> 00:19:33.966
And that means Team Orson wins the Pokémon Sky Relay.

359
00:19:35.766 --> 00:19:38.966
- Noibat.
- Noibat!

360
00:19:39.033 --> 00:19:41.200
Noi.

361
00:19:41.266 --> 00:19:43.366
Wow, Noibat, I'm so proud of you.

362
00:19:43.433 --> 00:19:46.933
You were so amazing. What a great last leg.

363
00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:48.933
Ha!

364
00:19:50.200 --> 00:19:52.433
Noi-oi!

365
00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:55.466
Fletchinder and Hawlucha, you were incredible too.

366
00:19:55.533 --> 00:19:57.233
Oh, what a close second.

367
00:19:57.300 --> 00:20:00.366
Don't forget that you were neck-and-neck with Team Orson.

368
00:20:00.433 --> 00:20:01.600
Denne-ne-ne-ne!

369
00:20:01.666 --> 00:20:03.933
I can't thank you enough, Ash.

370
00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:06.633
You've allowed me to finally live my dream.

371
00:20:06.700 --> 00:20:11.066
I'm deeply grateful to all of you. It's such a wonderful feeling!

372
00:20:12.566 --> 00:20:15.033
- Cha!
- Fletchinder!

373
00:20:15.100 --> 00:20:17.100
-Noibat!

374
00:20:23.066 --> 00:20:26.566
Team Orson has won the Sky Relay Cup.

375
00:20:26.633 --> 00:20:30.500
So let's give them a huge round of applause for a job well done.

376
00:20:32.566 --> 00:20:35.200
Team Orson may have won the Pokémon Sky Relay,

377
00:20:35.266 --> 00:20:38.666
but Noibat has gained valuable confidence and strength.

378
00:20:38.733 --> 00:20:43.533
And that means everybody's a winner, as the journey continues.
